  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Romans",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 6,
    "summary": "Baptism is in similitude of the death, burial, and resurrection of Christ—The wages of sin is death—Christ brings eternal life.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "What shall we say then? Shall we continue in sin, that grace may abound?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "D&C 20:32 (29–34)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "God forbid. How shall we, that are dead to sin, live any longer therein?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "GR May it not be!"
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "Mosiah 2:41."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Know ye not, that so many of us as were baptized into Jesus Christ were baptized into his death?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "Mosiah 27:25."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore we are buried with him by baptism into death: that like as Christ was raised up from the dead by the glory of the Father, even so we also should walk in newness of life.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "TG Baptism, Immersion."
          },
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG Baptism."
          },
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Death of."
          },
          {
            "start": 155,
            "end": 159,
            "text": "TG Walking with God."
          },
          {
            "start": 163,
            "end": 170,
            "text": "TG Baptism, Qualifications for; Man, New, Spiritually Reborn."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For if we have been planted together in the likeness of his death, we shall be also in the likeness of his resurrection:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Types of, in Memory."
          },
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 65,
            "text": "Col. 2:20; 3:3; 2 Tim. 2:11."
          },
          {
            "start": 107,
            "end": 119,
            "text": "TG Resurrection."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 99
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 106
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Knowing this, that our old man is crucified with him, that the body of sin might be destroyed, that henceforth we should not serve sin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "Eph. 4:22 (22–24); Col. 3:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 67,
            "text": "Col. 2:11."
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "GR brought to an end, freed."
          },
          {
            "start": 131,
            "end": 134,
            "text": "Moro. 10:32 (32–33)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For he that is dead is freed from sin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "JST Rom. 6:7 … dead to sin …"
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "GR acquitted, cleared."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Now if we be dead with Christ, we believe that we shall also live with him:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Death of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Knowing that Christ being raised from the dead dieth no more; death hath no more dominion over him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Resurrection."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For in that he died, he died unto sin once: but in that he liveth, he liveth unto God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "Heb. 9:28."
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "Heb. 7:27; 10:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Likewise reckon ye also yourselves to be dead indeed unto sin, but alive unto God through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "Gal. 2:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Let not sin therefore reign in your mortal body, that ye should obey it in the lusts thereof.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Mortality."
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 84,
            "text": "TG Lust."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Neither yield ye your members as instruments of unrighteousness unto sin: but yield yourselves unto God, as those that are alive from the dead, and your members as instruments of righteousness unto God.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "2 Ne. 4:27 (27–28)."
          },
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "Col. 3:5."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "GR weapons."
          },
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 83,
            "text": "Mosiah 3:19; Hel. 3:35."
          },
          {
            "start": 179,
            "end": 192,
            "text": "TG Righteousness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 32
          },
          {
            "start": 161,
            "end": 163
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For sin shall not have dominion over you: for ye are not under the law, but under grace.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "JST Rom. 6:14 For in so doing sin …"
          },
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "2 Ne. 2:29 (26–29)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "What then? shall we sin, because we are not under the law, but under grace? God forbid.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 74,
            "text": "TG Grace."
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "GR May it not be!"
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Know ye not, that to whom ye yield yourselves servants to obey, his servants ye are to whom ye obey; whether of sin unto death, or of obedience unto righteousness?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "John 8:34."
          },
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "Alma 3:27 (26–27); 34:34 (33–36); Hel. 14:31 (29–31). TG Obedience."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But God be thanked, that ye were the servants of sin, but ye have obeyed from the heart that form of doctrine which was delivered you.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "TG Commitment."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Being then made free from sin, ye became the servants of righteousness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "Mosiah 5:8 (7–8). TG Remission of Sins."
          },
          {
            "start": 26,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "TG Bondage, Spiritual; Sin."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I speak after the manner of men because of the infirmity of your flesh: for as ye have yielded your members servants to uncleanness and to iniquity unto iniquity; even so now yield your members servants to righteousness unto holiness.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For when ye were the servants of sin, ye were free from righteousness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "GR unrestricted by."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "What fruit had ye then in those things whereof ye are now ashamed? for the end of those things is death.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "GR benefit, reward."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 95,
            "end": 97
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But now being made free from sin, and become servants to God, ye have your fruit unto holiness, and the end everlasting life.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "Rom. 8:2 (1–4); Rev. 2:17 (17, 26)."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "GR benefit, reward."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 94,
            "text": "TG Sanctification."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For the wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "TG Wages."
          },
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "TG Sin."
          },
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 29,
            "text": "TG Death; Death, Spiritual, First."
          },
          {
            "start": 39,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG God, Gifts of."
          },
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Eternal Life."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 23
          },
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
